  <revision rev="2" vrev="1">
    <srcmd5>daa1337b2fb456a58adc3912cf5aee76</srcmd5>
    <version>276</version>
    <time>1795714335</time>
    <user>anag_factory</user>
    <comment>- Update to version 276:
  * peers can advertise their models automatically: llama-swap reads the
    peer's /v1/models instead of every model ID being listed in the
    configuration, so discovered models route, list and update without a
    restart or a configuration reload
  * peers.*.models accepts &quot;add &lt;regex&gt;&quot; and &quot;remove &lt;regex&gt;&quot; rules, applied
    from top to bottom, and a new peers.*.catalog block sets path, refresh,
    limit and transitive; catalogs are fetched in the background, are cached,
    and the last good list is kept when a fetch fails
  * new GET /api/peers and POST /api/peers/{peer}/refresh endpoints
  * the Models page is split into Local, Peers, Selectors and Profiles tabs
    that show counts, hide when empty and remember the chosen tab; the
    Profiles tab lists every configured profile with its description and
    mappings, so switching is one click
  * FastFlowLM throughput metrics (usage.prefill_speed_tps and
    usage.decoding_speed_tps) are read, so its throughput shows in the
    Activity view</comment>
    <requestid>1400860</requestid>
  </revision>
</revisionlist>
